<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">

<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0" />
    <meta name="theme-color" content="#FFFFFF" />
    <base href="/" />
    @* No static <title> here: every page supplies its own through <PageTitle>, and with
       prerendering the HeadOutlet emits a real <title> element into this head. A second,
       earlier one would win in the served HTML (browsers and crawlers take the first). *@
    <meta name="description" content="Bit.Blex is lightweight, source-generator-powered reactive state management for Blazor and .NET MAUI, with Redux DevTools time-travel, effects, persistence and undo/redo built in." />

    @* What a link to the site looks like when it is shared. *@
    <meta property="og:type" content="website" />
    <meta property="og:site_name" content="Bit.Blex" />
    <meta property="og:title" content="Blex - reactive state management for Blazor" />
    <meta property="og:description" content="One [BlexState] field, one [BlexAction] method. No reducers, no boilerplate - and Redux DevTools time-travel out of the box." />
    <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary" />

    <ResourcePreloader />
    @* The site kit (app.css, theme.js, site.js - shared by every Utilities demo), then this demo's
       own sample styles. *@
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="@Assets["app.css"]" />
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="@Assets["demo.css"]" />
    @* Scoped-CSS bundle: includes the client project's *.razor.css files as well. *@
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="@Assets["Bit.Blex.Demo.Server.styles.css"]" />
    @* Synchronous on purpose: applies the light/dark theme before first paint. *@
    <script src="@Assets["theme.js"]"></script>
    <ImportMap />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="favicon.svg" />
    @* Same render mode as the app itself, so <PageTitle> keeps working after hydration. *@
    <HeadOutlet @rendermode="InteractiveWebAssembly" />
</head>

<body>
    @* Prerendered on the server, then hydrated by the WebAssembly runtime. Stores render their
       initial state in the served HTML; <BlexProvider> hands that state to the interactive render
       and then rehydrates the persisted stores from localStorage. Bit.Blex has no stylesheet, and
       its two script modules are imported on demand by the persistence and DevTools bridges. *@
    <Routes @rendermode="InteractiveWebAssembly" />

    <div id="blazor-error-ui" data-nosnippet>
        An unhandled error has occurred.
        <a href="." class="reload">Reload</a>
        <span class="dismiss">&#128473;</span>
    </div>

    <script src="@Assets["_framework/blazor.web.js"]"></script>
    <script src="@Assets["site.js"]"></script>
    @* The one helper a page needs beyond the kit: the persistence page reads the raw payload Blex
       wrote to localStorage. *@
    <script src="@Assets["demo.js"]"></script>
</body>

</html>
